#. type: Content of: <div><div><p>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:5
msgid "DI, REST controllers, data repositories, <code>application.properties</code> &mdash; many Spring concepts map neatly to Quarkus equivalents. You can get your Spring applications running on Quarkus by making (small!) adjustments to code that interacts with the framework, or by using compatibility libraries. Whichever way you go, there's lots of help available, including AI skills, migration tooling, and documentation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><h2>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:13
msgid "AI-Driven Migration"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><p>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:14
msgid "<strong>AI skills</strong> give a coding agent a structured task to follow — the <strong>Quarkus Migration Skill</strong> does that for a Spring Boot to Quarkus migration. Point it at your app, and it inspects your codebase, migrates what applies — build files, REST controllers, dependency injection, data access, security, configuration, tests — flagging decisions for you along the way, then commits the result and opens a draft PR."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><p>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:15
msgid "<strong>Best for:</strong> anyone who wants a concrete answer to &ldquo;what would this actually take?&rdquo; &mdash; on a real service, in an afternoon."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><pre>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:17
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>npx skills add quarkusio/skills</code>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><p>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:18
msgid "From your project root, prompt your agent: &ldquo;Migrate this Spring Boot app to Quarkus.&rdquo;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><p>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:19
msgid "You can choose to use either target &mdash; native Quarkus APIs or Spring compatibility extensions (covered next)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><p>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:20
msgid "<i class=\"fa fa-chevron-right\"></i><a href=\"https://github.com/quarkusio/skills#migrate-spring-to-quarkus\">Get the Quarkus Migration Skill </a>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><h3>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:22
msgid "Also in the AI-assisted family"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><div><div><div><div><h5>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:27
msgid "General AI coding assistants"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><div><div><div><div><p>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:28
msgid "Claude Code, Cursor, GitHub Copilot, Bob, and other coding assistants can translate Spring code with the right prompts. Konveyor AI adds IDE-integrated static analysis for teams already using Konveyor or MTA."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><div><div><div><div><p>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:29
msgid "<i class=\"fa fa-chevron-right\"></i><a href=\"https://www.the-main-thread.com/p/spring-to-quarkus-migration-guide\">Hands-on walkthrough</a>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><div><div><div><div><h5>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:36
msgid "Konveyor AI (Kai)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><div><div><div><div><p>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:37
msgid "Combines generative AI with static code analysis to assist migration directly in your IDE. Uses a RAG-based approach with historical migration data to provide context-specific guidance, without requiring model fine-tuning."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><div><div><div><div><p>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:38
msgid "<i class=\"fa fa-chevron-right\"></i><a href=\"https://konveyor.github.io/components/kai/\">Learn about Konveyor AI</a>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><h2>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:50
msgid "Two destinations, your choice"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><p>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:51
msgid "Whichever tools you use, there&rsquo;s one decision to make: what should the migrated code look like? You can start with one and move to the other incrementally."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><div><div><h3>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:55
msgid "Native Quarkus APIs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><div><div><p>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:56
msgid "Migrate to Quarkus&rsquo;s own APIs: Jakarta REST for endpoints, CDI for dependency injection, Panache for data access. The concepts are the ones you already know &mdash; <code>@Inject</code> instead of <code>@Autowired</code>, <code>@Path</code> instead of <code>@RequestMapping</code>, and so on. In our experience most teams adapt to the new APIs quickly."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><div><div><p>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:57
msgid "<strong>What you gain:</strong> the full performance of Quarkus &mdash; faster startup, lower memory, first-class native compilation &mdash; plus idiomatic code that most Quarkus guide, extension, and community answers are written for."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><div><div><p>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:58
msgid "<strong>Best for:</strong> new services, services you&rsquo;ll maintain for years, and teams ready to invest a small amount of learning for the full payoff. This is where most migrations end up &mdash; the only question is whether you go there directly."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><div><div><p>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:59
msgid "<strong>Trade-off:</strong> some parts of your codebase will look less familiar, and the diff for the migration will be larger."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><div><div><h3>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:62
msgid "Spring compatibility extensions"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><div><div><p>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:63
msgid "Keep your Spring annotations and patterns &mdash; <code>@RestController</code>, <code>@Autowired</code>, <code>JpaRepository</code>, but running on the Quarkus runtime. The build plugin and BOM change, property names change, but your code largely stays as it is. The best bit? Your code doesn't change, but its performance does. A lot. (For the better!)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><div><div><p>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:64
msgid "<strong>What you gain:</strong> the quickest route to Quarkus with near-zero code cognitive load. Your team stays productive on day one while still getting a leaner, faster application."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><div><div><p>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:65
msgid "<strong>Best for:</strong> getting a service onto Quarkus fast, teams that can&rsquo;t absorb any extra learning right now, and as a first step in an incremental migration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><div><div><p>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:66
msgid "<strong>Trade-off:</strong> coverage isn&rsquo;t total, and you leave some performance and ecosystem benefits on the table until you complete the move to Quarkus's own APIs."
msgstr ""

