#. type: Content of: <div><div><h2>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:125
msgid "Deterministic and specialized tools"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><p>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:126
msgid "The Migration Skill handles the general case. These tools shine in particular ones &mdash; large portfolios, bulk mechanical changes, or when you want to understand every rule yourself."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><table><thead><tr><th>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:131
#, fuzzy
msgid "Tool"
msgstr "工具"

#. type: Content of: <div><div><table><thead><tr><th>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:132
msgid "What it does"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><table><thead><tr><th>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:133
msgid "Best for"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><table><tbody><tr><td>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:138
msgid "<strong><a href=\"{=''}/blog/migrating-existing-apps-to-quarkus-with-mta/\">Migration Toolkit for Applications (MTA)</a></strong>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><table><tbody><tr><td>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:139
msgid "Rule-based analysis (built on <a href=\"https://www.konveyor.io/\">Konveyor</a>) that reports exactly what needs to change in your app, with guidance for each issue. Web console, CLI, Maven plugin, or IDE plugin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><table><tbody><tr><td>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:140
msgid "Sizing the effort across a large portfolio before committing; teams that need an assessment report for planning or stakeholders."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><table><tbody><tr><td>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:143
msgid "<strong><a href=\"https://docs.openrewrite.org/recipes/quarkus/spring/springboottoquarkus\">OpenRewrite</a></strong>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><table><tbody><tr><td>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:144
msgid "The <code>SpringBootToQuarkus</code> recipe automates dependency swaps, annotation changes, and configuration migration deterministically via Maven, Gradle, or CLI."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><table><tbody><tr><td>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:145
msgid "Applying the same mechanical changes across many similar services; teams that prefer repeatable, rule-based transforms over AI."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><table><tbody><tr><td>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:148
msgid "<strong><a href=\"https://github.com/snowdrop/springboot-to-quarkus-migration-guide\">Snowdrop Migration Guide</a></strong>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><table><tbody><tr><td>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:149
msgid "A structured manual guide with rules and decision flowcharts for Spring Boot 3.x Quarkus 3.x, covering both destination strategies. Includes Konveyor analysis rules."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><table><tbody><tr><td>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:150
msgid "Understanding exactly what changes and why; handling edge cases that automation misses."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><h2>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:161
msgid "Common questions"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><dl><dt>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:164
msgid "Do I have to migrate everything at once?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><dl><dd><p>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:165
msgid "No. Migrate one service, and within it, run compatibility extensions and native APIs side by side &mdash; incrementally, even class by class, as it suits you."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><dl><dt>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:167
msgid "How much do I have to relearn for Quarkus-native APIs?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><dl><dd><p>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:168
msgid "Not much &mdash; <code>@Inject</code> instead of <code>@Autowired</code>, <code>@Path</code> instead of <code>@RequestMapping</code>. Most developers are productive within days."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><dl><dt>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:170
msgid "Is the Quarkus ecosystem mature enough?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><dl><dd><p>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:171
msgid "Quarkus has hundreds of extensions built on proven projects like Hibernate, Vert.x, and RESTEasy, with a large, active community behind it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><dl><dt>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:173
msgid "What if my app uses Spring features the compatibility extensions don&rsquo;t cover?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><dl><dd><p>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:174
msgid "You migrate just those parts to their Quarkus equivalents &mdash; everything else can stay on compatibility extensions."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><dl><dt>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:176
msgid "Can I combine these tools?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><dl><dd><p>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:177
msgid "Yes &mdash; many teams run MTA first to scope the effort, then use the Migration Skill or OpenRewrite to do the work."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><dl><dt>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:179
msgid "Where do I start?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><dl><dd><p>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:180
msgid "Run the Quarkus Migration Skill on one service and review the draft PR it opens."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><div><p>
#: templates/partials/spring-migrate-content.html:183
msgid "For more guidance, the free <a href=\"https://developers.redhat.com/e-books/quarkus-spring-developers\" aria-label=\"Quarkus for Spring Developers free link\">Quarkus for Spring Developers e-book</a> explains the similarities and differences between the two frameworks, and helps you map Spring Boot concepts to their Quarkus equivalents."
msgstr ""
